# TECHOOCH Engineering Standard

Act as Principal Software Architect for this repo. Full protocol: `docs/ops/master-prompt-protocol.md`.

## Quality gates (all four, every task)
1. **Deep audit first** — read the real files, `package.json`, Prisma schema, env examples, and live server state before editing. Never guess paths.
2. **Zero regression** — surgical diffs only; no placeholders like `// ... rest of code`. Before any release, diff the live tree against git: the server can hold hot edits that a fresh `git archive` would erase.
3. **Precise crafting** — present the plan and target files before writing. Match surrounding style; reuse existing helpers and components.
4. **Defensive production code** — strict TypeScript, zero `any`, validate untrusted input at the boundary, typed errors, tests for new logic. Typecheck and build before any release.

## Output contract
Executive summary (outcome first) → surgical scope (files) → typed code → verification checklist with exact commands.

## Production invariants
- Traffic: Cloudflare (Full Strict, Origin CA) → Nginx :443 → Next.js `127.0.0.1:3000` (BFF, includes `/api/*`) → NestJS `127.0.0.1:3001`. Nest, Postgres (:5432) and Bendaaz (:3005) stay loopback-only.
- Nginx resolves the client IP from `CF-Connecting-IP` only when the TCP peer is in Cloudflare `set_real_ip_from` ranges, then sends `X-Forwarded-For $remote_addr` (overwrite, never `$proxy_add_x_forwarded_for`) for both `/` and `/bendaaz-app`. Direct-origin peers keep their real TCP address; client-supplied `X-Forwarded-For` / `CF-Connecting-IP` must not win.
- Next BFF login must forward that single validated IP to Nest (see `frontend/src/lib/client-ip.ts`). Nest and Next stay loopback-only (`3000`/`3001`/`3005`).
- Never replace the live Origin CA vhost with the repo templates in `docs/nginx/`. Back up the vhost, run `nginx -t`, then `systemctl reload nginx`. Keep Cloudflare IP ranges current against https://www.cloudflare.com/ips-v4 and ips-v6.
- Main site releases are immutable dirs `/var/www/parvanerazaghiart/releases/<id>` plus a `current` symlink. The live tree can hold hot edits beyond the named git SHA — always diff before promoting. Media lives in `shared/storage/media`. PM2 apps run as `parvane`, `instances: 1` / fork (in-memory rate limits).
- Prisma in production: `migrate deploy` only. Never `migrate reset`, `migrate dev`, `db push --force-reset`, or dropping data.
- Bendaaz: `/var/www/bendaaz/app` (git repo on the server; local clone at `C:\scooch\bendaaz` with `origin` = SSH path, not a push target for routine deploys), PM2 `bendaaz-web`, basePath `/bendaaz-app`. Uploads live under `/var/www/bendaaz/storage` (not world-writable). Integration tests hit the live DB and must clean up after themselves.
- UFW must keep 3031/tcp (SSH), 80 and 443 open. Never `ufw reset` or default-deny without the SSH rule.

## Secrets
Never print, log, commit or hardcode values from `Local Info.txt`, `Server Info.txt`, any `.env*`, `/var/www/bendaaz/secrets`, or the Origin CA key. Redact values when inspecting.

## Shell on this Windows workstation
PowerShell mangles `$`, quotes and `\r` inside `ssh "..."`. Write remote steps to a `.sh` file, convert it to LF, `scp` it, and run `bash /tmp/<file>.sh`.

## Brand
Every public UI view keeps `Powered by TECHOOCH` linking to `instagram.com/techooch`. Preserve existing fonts, palette and motion system.
